1
00:00:01,679 --> 00:00:03,180
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:34,021
ALGAMA BOTANICAL GARDEN

3
00:01:35,356 --> 00:01:37,566
{\an8}EMPLOYEES ONLY
BACK ENTRANCE

4
00:01:37,650 --> 00:01:39,693
{\an8}UDON BEBEBE

5
00:01:44,907 --> 00:01:48,160
{\an8}[Legoshi] I'm from Udon Bebebe.
I'm here to pick up the bowls.

6
00:01:49,411 --> 00:01:50,246
[Legoshi grunts]

7
00:01:50,329 --> 00:01:51,330
[rustling]

8
00:01:51,413 --> 00:01:52,790
[female staff screams]

9
00:01:52,873 --> 00:01:56,210
- [female staff grunts in pain]
- [Legoshi] Huh? Ah, are you all right?

10
00:01:56,293 --> 00:01:59,255
[female staff]
Am I all right? Did you see that fall?

11
00:01:59,338 --> 00:02:01,382
I let a butterfly escape.

12
00:02:01,465 --> 00:02:02,716
[Legoshi] A butterfly?

13
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,677
I've been waiting for it to come out.

14
00:02:05,177 --> 00:02:07,263
[Legoshi] Uh... [inhales]

15
00:02:07,346 --> 00:02:09,807
So, um, would you like me
to help you find it?

16
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:12,643
- Huh?
- Well, tell me what it looks like.

17
00:02:13,144 --> 00:02:15,813
{\an8}It's blue.
And it's got wings about this wide.

18
00:02:15,896 --> 00:02:17,439
{\an8}Ah. A Ulysses butterfly.

19
00:02:17,523 --> 00:02:20,860
{\an8}Uh... No, it's a morpho butterfly.

20
00:02:20,943 --> 00:02:22,653
Oh, one of those. Hmm.

21
00:02:22,736 --> 00:02:24,822
Um...

22
00:02:26,699 --> 00:02:27,533
Hmm.

23
00:02:27,616 --> 00:02:30,369
- Oh. Can I borrow this jar?
- [female staff] I guess.

24
00:02:30,452 --> 00:02:32,163
Do you have any aluminum foil?

25
00:02:32,246 --> 00:02:35,583
{\an8}Uh, yeah.
Stay here, just give me a second. [grunts]

26
00:02:38,294 --> 00:02:39,420
[door closes]

27
00:02:42,965 --> 00:02:46,135
[Legoshi] Morpho butterflies
are attracted to blue reflections.

28
00:02:46,218 --> 00:02:47,928
Oh, good to know!

29
00:02:48,012 --> 00:02:50,139
[Legoshi] Yeah, they think
it's one of their own.

30
00:02:50,764 --> 00:02:55,686
You know, they also really like
sugarcane juice and over-ripened fruit.

31
00:02:55,769 --> 00:02:56,604
[ethereal shimmering]

32
00:02:56,687 --> 00:02:57,521
Hey!

33
00:02:57,605 --> 00:03:00,274
[gasps] Look at that!

34
00:03:00,357 --> 00:03:02,151
[Legoshi] Oh, wow.

35
00:03:02,735 --> 00:03:04,528
It's so beautiful.

36
00:03:05,279 --> 00:03:07,323
[female staff] It really is, isn't it?

37
00:03:08,616 --> 00:03:10,409
[Legoshi] All right, get your net.
You ready?

38
00:03:10,492 --> 00:03:11,493
[female staff] Oh. Oh, yeah, right.

39
00:03:11,577 --> 00:03:13,871
- [exhales]
- [ethereal shimmering]

40
00:03:13,954 --> 00:03:15,205
[grunts with effort] Ah!

41
00:03:15,289 --> 00:03:16,749
Nice catch!

42
00:03:16,832 --> 00:03:18,751
Ah. [laughs exultantly]

43
00:03:18,834 --> 00:03:21,629
You really saved me.
You are a butterfly whisperer.

44
00:03:21,712 --> 00:03:23,088
[laughs sheepishly]

45
00:03:23,172 --> 00:03:26,050
I wish! Just a hobby of mine. [inhales]

46
00:03:26,133 --> 00:03:28,302
Ever think about coming to work here?

47
00:03:28,385 --> 00:03:30,012
I can get you an application. Huh?

48
00:03:30,095 --> 00:03:32,431
Oh, no. I'm good.

49
00:03:32,514 --> 00:03:34,350
Someone has to deliver the noodles.

50
00:03:34,433 --> 00:03:36,185
You can think about it, right?

51
00:03:36,268 --> 00:03:37,937
Yeah. I will.

52
00:03:38,896 --> 00:03:39,772
Hmm.

53
00:03:40,773 --> 00:03:43,776
<i>Well, it would be
a pretty nice place to work.</i>

54
00:03:44,985 --> 00:03:49,907
SIX TAILS IN A ROW

55
00:03:52,117 --> 00:03:53,661
And I'm back!

56
00:03:53,744 --> 00:03:55,955
[Sunaga grunts with exertion]
You took long enough.

57
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:57,623
Let's get moving.

58
00:03:57,706 --> 00:04:00,793
You wanna make up for your sick leave,
I need you to work a little harder.

59
00:04:00,876 --> 00:04:02,795
Those dishes are ready.
Tempura for table two.

60
00:04:02,878 --> 00:04:05,464
- [Legoshi] Yeah. Got it.
- [Sunaga] Wait! Not that one.

61
00:04:05,547 --> 00:04:06,757
Look at the order notes.

62
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,008
{\an8}[Legoshi] Oh, sorry.

63
00:04:08,092 --> 00:04:10,970
{\an8}[Sunaga] Table two is canine.
We can't serve them onions.

64
00:04:11,053 --> 00:04:12,096
{\an8}[Legoshi] Oh, yeah, I see.

65
00:04:12,179 --> 00:04:13,222
{\an8}Be careful.

66
00:04:13,305 --> 00:04:16,225
{\an8}We're not gonna stay in business
if we're getting carnivores sick.

67
00:04:16,308 --> 00:04:17,351
Right. You're right.

68
00:04:17,434 --> 00:04:18,811
- [horn honking]
- [vehicle passing]

69
00:04:18,894 --> 00:04:20,896
[Sunaga] Oh. Almost forgot.

70
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:22,898
You got a call from a friend.

71
00:04:22,982 --> 00:04:25,651
Really? Which one?

72
00:04:27,903 --> 00:04:32,574
[indistinct chatter]

73
00:04:32,658 --> 00:04:34,535
[Fudge] Guys! Hearing anything good?

74
00:04:35,077 --> 00:04:37,413
{\an8}[sighs in exasperation]
Go shut that guy up.

75
00:04:37,496 --> 00:04:38,539
{\an8}Um...

76
00:04:39,081 --> 00:04:40,082
{\an8}FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR SCRIPT

77
00:04:40,165 --> 00:04:43,419
{\an8}[Gon] Your script for the new stage play.
I read it.

78
00:04:44,628 --> 00:04:46,463
Personally, I think plays

79
00:04:46,547 --> 00:04:50,050
about friendships
between carnivores and herbivores

80
00:04:50,134 --> 00:04:53,470
aren't nearly
as palatable as they once were.

81
00:04:53,554 --> 00:04:55,306
[both sigh]

82
00:04:55,389 --> 00:04:56,849
[Gon] But this one's different.

83
00:04:56,932 --> 00:05:00,394
You are trying to overcome
those old tropes and cliches, right?

84
00:05:00,477 --> 00:05:01,395
Right.

85
00:05:01,478 --> 00:05:02,604
[Gon] Hmm.

86
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:06,608
Don't you worry.
I'll handle things with the committee.

87
00:05:06,692 --> 00:05:07,860
[Els] So that means...

88
00:05:07,943 --> 00:05:10,070
So that means you can stage your play.

89
00:05:10,154 --> 00:05:11,947
- [Bill laughing] Yes!
- [Els laughing]

90
00:05:12,031 --> 00:05:12,990
Hang on, calm down now.

91
00:05:13,073 --> 00:05:14,575
- We still have rules here.
- [Els] Uh...

92
00:05:14,658 --> 00:05:16,535
Oh, right. Sorry, sir.

93
00:05:17,369 --> 00:05:19,163
This has real potential.

94
00:05:19,246 --> 00:05:22,207
A touching friendship
between fangs and horns.

95
00:05:22,291 --> 00:05:25,294
"Our love is an oasis in the arid desert."

96
00:05:25,377 --> 00:05:26,378
Nice line!

97
00:05:26,462 --> 00:05:27,921
[chuckling] Yes!

98
00:05:28,005 --> 00:05:29,840
We did it!

99
00:05:29,923 --> 00:05:31,258
[Ellen] It's taking too long.

100
00:05:31,341 --> 00:05:34,219
[sighs] It's my fault
if it doesn't work out.

101
00:05:34,303 --> 00:05:36,221
Didn't you say you were confident?

102
00:05:36,305 --> 00:05:37,431
- [Ellen] Oh!
- [all grunting]

103
00:05:37,514 --> 00:05:38,557
[Kibi] Wait for me!

104
00:05:39,266 --> 00:05:40,559
- [Fudge] Oh, boy.
- [others gasp]

105
00:05:40,642 --> 00:05:42,644
[indistinct chatter]

106
00:05:48,734 --> 00:05:49,651
[Gon] Hmm...

107
00:05:52,571 --> 00:05:55,949
Festival of the Meteor.
Certainly exciting.

108
00:05:56,450 --> 00:05:58,494
- [all speaking indistinctly]
- [door closes]

109
00:05:58,577 --> 00:06:01,246
[all cheering]

110
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:05,459
- We did it, Tao buddy!
- Oh, man, it's all thanks to you!

111
00:06:05,542 --> 00:06:08,545
- Oh, I'd give you a hug if I could!
- Well, let's get this wall out of here!

112
00:06:08,629 --> 00:06:10,380
It's in the way of us building set pieces.

113
00:06:10,464 --> 00:06:11,840
- [Bill] Not so fast.
- [Fudge] Huh?

114
00:06:11,924 --> 00:06:14,051
- [Bill] Doesn't work that way.
- [Kai] Why not?

115
00:06:14,134 --> 00:06:17,888
During the prep period, we are supposed
to remain as two separate clubs.

116
00:06:17,971 --> 00:06:21,475
We can't avoid it during performance,
but until then we stay separated.

117
00:06:21,558 --> 00:06:24,061
- [Fudge] Seriously?
- [Els] We still have our rules.

118
00:06:24,144 --> 00:06:26,271
Let's be grateful we got approval.

119
00:06:26,355 --> 00:06:29,108
Thanks to Kibi and Tao
for writing such a great script.

120
00:06:29,191 --> 00:06:30,567
[gentle applause]

121
00:06:30,651 --> 00:06:31,860
Well...

122
00:06:31,944 --> 00:06:34,488
- You rock!
- Come on now, that's enough.

123
00:06:34,571 --> 00:06:35,781
Thank you, guys.

124
00:06:35,864 --> 00:06:39,535
You know, from here on out,
we are all gonna to have to step it up.

125
00:06:40,202 --> 00:06:42,371
I think Juno should play the lead role.

126
00:06:42,454 --> 00:06:44,039
The carnivore protagonist.

127
00:06:44,123 --> 00:06:45,624
- What do you say?
- [Juno] What?

128
00:06:45,707 --> 00:06:47,835
[inhales] Okay!

129
00:06:47,918 --> 00:06:51,130
[Ellen] So let's figure out
who will play the herbivore hero.

130
00:06:51,755 --> 00:06:54,091
For a story about friendship
between horns and fangs,

131
00:06:54,174 --> 00:06:56,385
it would be best
to pick someone with horns.

132
00:06:57,594 --> 00:06:58,595
Pina can do it.

133
00:06:59,763 --> 00:07:01,640
Pina's horns would really stand out.

134
00:07:01,723 --> 00:07:03,600
Even though
his last performance got canceled,

135
00:07:04,101 --> 00:07:07,771
I think we can all agree,
he was really good in rehearsals.

136
00:07:07,855 --> 00:07:10,983
So that's why, I would nominate him.

137
00:07:11,066 --> 00:07:12,860
[exhales] I agree.

138
00:07:12,943 --> 00:07:14,903
But he quit the club, right?

139
00:07:14,987 --> 00:07:17,948
He quit
because we were forced to stay separate.

140
00:07:18,031 --> 00:07:21,034
But now we have approval
to work together. Right? Right?

141
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:24,496
I don't know.
I'm not sure I can convince him.

142
00:07:25,122 --> 00:07:26,373
We can try.

143
00:07:26,457 --> 00:07:28,292
Let's see, how about this?

144
00:07:28,375 --> 00:07:30,502
- Hey, Juno!
- Me?

145
00:07:30,586 --> 00:07:35,340
[Bill] You are in the same year as Pina.
Maybe he can be convinced by his costar.

146
00:07:35,424 --> 00:07:37,801
Also, he'll listen to a girl.

147
00:07:37,885 --> 00:07:40,095
He'll at least consider your invitation.

148
00:07:40,179 --> 00:07:41,889
[Juno] Uh, yeah, but...

149
00:07:41,972 --> 00:07:43,515
[Bill] Listen up.

150
00:07:43,599 --> 00:07:47,519
The first step on the long journey
towards getting this show off the ground

151
00:07:47,603 --> 00:07:50,022
is get Pina back on board.

152
00:07:50,105 --> 00:07:51,690
Uh... Uh...

153
00:07:51,773 --> 00:07:55,944
Juno, the success
of the Festival of the Meteor

154
00:07:56,028 --> 00:07:57,654
now rests on your shoulders!

155
00:07:57,738 --> 00:08:02,159
- Me? Well, uh...
- [Els] Juno, we can count on you, right?

156
00:08:02,993 --> 00:08:05,579
{\an8}Uh... Yes.

157
00:08:07,706 --> 00:08:10,292
<i>Why would it have to be Pina
of all people?</i>

158
00:08:10,375 --> 00:08:12,211
<i>He quit the club!</i>

159
00:08:12,294 --> 00:08:15,172
<i>He skipped rehearsals,
he was disrespectful to classmates,</i>

160
00:08:15,255 --> 00:08:18,050
<i>his ridiculously well-groomed fur,
give me a break!</i>

161
00:08:18,133 --> 00:08:19,593
Coming to the herbivore floor?

162
00:08:19,676 --> 00:08:20,928
The old rooftop should be empty.

163
00:08:21,011 --> 00:08:23,013
Okay, there then!

164
00:08:25,224 --> 00:08:26,350
[Juno sighing in irritation]

165
00:08:26,433 --> 00:08:28,519
<i>I kind of hope he doesn't show up.</i>

166
00:08:29,603 --> 00:08:31,188
GARDENING CLUB

167
00:08:35,442 --> 00:08:37,444
[Juno] <i>Oh, that's right.</i>

168
00:08:38,153 --> 00:08:39,905
<i>This club was shut down.</i>

169
00:08:45,077 --> 00:08:46,995
[Haru] I really appreciate the help.

170
00:08:47,079 --> 00:08:49,289
I didn't think you would actually say yes.

171
00:08:50,123 --> 00:08:53,168
[Juno] <i>We went through all that effort
to plant these together...</i>

172
00:08:53,252 --> 00:08:55,712
<i>Coming to water them
is the least I could have done.</i>

173
00:08:56,421 --> 00:08:57,923
[Pina] So what's all this?

174
00:08:58,006 --> 00:09:01,218
Is gardening going to be
one of your new hobbies or something?

175
00:09:01,301 --> 00:09:03,053
That's a little surprising.

176
00:09:03,136 --> 00:09:05,847
I wouldn't necessarily say
I'm into gardening,

177
00:09:05,931 --> 00:09:08,183
but I appreciate the effort
that goes into it.

178
00:09:08,267 --> 00:09:11,770
[Pina] I suppose a club is nothing
without its members, eh?

179
00:09:11,853 --> 00:09:12,813
[scoffs]

180
00:09:12,896 --> 00:09:15,357
Suddenly hearing from you out of the blue
was a surprise.

181
00:09:15,983 --> 00:09:19,820
Let me guess. You're wanting me
to come back to the drama club.

182
00:09:20,404 --> 00:09:21,822
Well-- I mean...

183
00:09:22,447 --> 00:09:25,200
Well, you are short
on herbivore actors, right?

184
00:09:25,284 --> 00:09:26,243
[chuckles]

185
00:09:26,326 --> 00:09:28,829
Or maybe you just wanted to ask me out.

186
00:09:28,912 --> 00:09:30,080
What?

187
00:09:30,163 --> 00:09:31,290
[laughs dismissively]

188
00:09:31,373 --> 00:09:34,459
No, don't be silly.
You are right about the club.

189
00:09:35,210 --> 00:09:36,295
For the festival,

190
00:09:36,378 --> 00:09:40,007
we have permission to let carnivores
and herbivores perform together.

191
00:09:40,591 --> 00:09:41,592
Here's the thing.

192
00:09:41,675 --> 00:09:44,261
There's a really great role for you
in this script.

193
00:09:44,344 --> 00:09:48,390
{\an8}The role's a double lead,
and I would be your costar.

194
00:09:48,473 --> 00:09:51,852
<i>Come on, Juno. This is on you.
You've got to convince him!</i>

195
00:09:51,935 --> 00:09:53,020
FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR SCRIPT

196
00:09:53,103 --> 00:09:55,272
<i>This play needs Pina to pull off the lead.</i>

197
00:09:55,355 --> 00:09:58,233
<i>And now everyone thinks
this is all up to me,</i>

198
00:09:58,317 --> 00:10:00,152
<i>that I can pull this thing off.</i>

199
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,072
But I get it,
you are probably too busy, right?

200
00:10:04,156 --> 00:10:05,115
- Huh?
- You know, it's okay.

201
00:10:05,198 --> 00:10:07,534
It's not like it's
an end-of-the-world thing or something.

202
00:10:07,618 --> 00:10:09,328
I bet you've got a lot going on.

203
00:10:09,411 --> 00:10:12,164
I'll just let everyone know
you are into gardening now.

204
00:10:12,247 --> 00:10:15,000
Come on. I have plenty of free time.

205
00:10:15,083 --> 00:10:17,085
- Oh.
- [chuckling] I get it.

206
00:10:17,169 --> 00:10:20,839
My guess is the club seniors asked you
to come here and convince me.

207
00:10:20,922 --> 00:10:22,841
But I bet you yourself don't want me back.

208
00:10:23,467 --> 00:10:25,469
{\an8}[chuckles] Because if I'm there,

209
00:10:25,552 --> 00:10:27,846
{\an8}the spotlight on you
won't shine as bright.

210
00:10:28,347 --> 00:10:29,848
- Unbelievable.
- [mischievous music playing]

211
00:10:29,931 --> 00:10:32,017
Something I've noticed about you.

212
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:35,270
You are the type
who isn't afraid to play dirty.

213
00:10:36,063 --> 00:10:40,150
You'll do anything
to get exactly what you want.

214
00:10:40,233 --> 00:10:42,194
Huh, you've got some nerve!

215
00:10:42,277 --> 00:10:44,529
It doesn't matter to me
if you come back or not.

216
00:10:44,613 --> 00:10:45,781
- I don't need you to do me...
- Oh.

217
00:10:45,864 --> 00:10:46,698
...some kind of favor!

218
00:10:46,782 --> 00:10:49,618
I've got more than enough skills and looks
to outshine you any day.

219
00:10:49,701 --> 00:10:50,702
Wow.

220
00:10:51,244 --> 00:10:54,122
So you are dropping
your harmless carnivore act for me.

221
00:10:54,206 --> 00:10:56,500
I insist you drop yours first.

222
00:10:56,583 --> 00:10:58,669
You play it safe because you are afraid

223
00:10:58,752 --> 00:11:01,088
if you give it your all and you fail,
then what?

224
00:11:01,171 --> 00:11:04,508
If I give it my all,
it's you that's gonna be afraid.

225
00:11:04,591 --> 00:11:05,926
[scoffs] You wish.

226
00:11:06,009 --> 00:11:07,761
In rehearsals, you could be fantastic,

227
00:11:07,844 --> 00:11:09,346
but if you can't deliver on stage,
so what?

228
00:11:09,429 --> 00:11:11,348
Like you've ever seen me on stage.

229
00:11:11,431 --> 00:11:13,392
I bet you were relieved
when the last show got canceled.

230
00:11:13,475 --> 00:11:15,227
Were you the one behind that?

231
00:11:15,310 --> 00:11:18,522
[chuckles softly] Awful lot of effort
just to avoid being near me.

232
00:11:19,189 --> 00:11:21,650
Thank you, but I'll have to decline.

233
00:11:22,567 --> 00:11:25,487
Well, that's fine by me,
because I decline!

234
00:11:26,613 --> 00:11:27,447
[stage light switches on]

235
00:11:27,531 --> 00:11:30,367
We need to stop
this insufferable fighting!

236
00:11:30,450 --> 00:11:35,705
Our inexhaustible well of love
is our oasis in this arid desert!

237
00:11:35,789 --> 00:11:38,917
- We were so right to get Pina for this!
- Yeah.

238
00:11:40,210 --> 00:11:44,131
[Juno] <i>Unbelievable!
I wish he really had declined!</i>

239
00:11:51,221 --> 00:11:53,348
[Melon]
<i>When you are on a university campus,</i>

240
00:11:53,432 --> 00:11:56,226
<i>you get to witness
such interesting things.</i>

241
00:11:56,309 --> 00:11:57,394
[male hyena] Hey, what's up?

242
00:11:58,145 --> 00:12:00,480
Here are your notes from last week.
You are awesome.

243
00:12:00,564 --> 00:12:03,316
- Does it all make sense?
- Sure.

244
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:05,902
You wouldn't happen to have microeconomics
for me?

245
00:12:05,986 --> 00:12:08,280
- [female deer] Well...
- [Melon] <i>They are no longer children,</i>

246
00:12:08,363 --> 00:12:09,906
<i>and not quite adults.</i>

247
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:12,659
<i>But when carnivores interact
with herbivores,</i>

248
00:12:12,742 --> 00:12:14,578
<i>their true nature reveals itself.</i>

249
00:12:15,579 --> 00:12:19,833
<i>The carnivore's gaze finds its way
to the most appetizing parts.</i>

250
00:12:19,916 --> 00:12:22,586
<i>While the herbivore remains
wholly unaware.</i>

251
00:12:24,212 --> 00:12:25,213
[female deer] Here.

252
00:12:25,297 --> 00:12:27,674
Oh, uh, yeah. Thanks a lot.

253
00:12:27,757 --> 00:12:30,427
- [Melon] <i>This eternal dynamic...</i>
- Later then.

254
00:12:31,136 --> 00:12:32,846
[Melon] <i>...it makes me jealous.</i>

255
00:12:33,388 --> 00:12:38,310
<i>Eating meat after struggling so long
to suppress your instincts...</i>

256
00:12:38,393 --> 00:12:41,146
<i>It must taste twice as sweet.</i>

257
00:12:41,980 --> 00:12:42,898
[knock on door]

258
00:12:43,899 --> 00:12:44,983
Yes?

259
00:12:45,066 --> 00:12:47,777
It's Haru, the freshman studying botany.

260
00:12:47,861 --> 00:12:48,862
[Melon] Mmm.

261
00:12:49,488 --> 00:12:50,322
Come in.

262
00:12:52,324 --> 00:12:53,533
Hope I'm not a bother.

263
00:12:53,617 --> 00:12:55,410
[Melon] Ah, hello again.

264
00:12:59,498 --> 00:13:00,582
Have a seat.

265
00:13:02,542 --> 00:13:04,211
Thank you very much.

266
00:13:07,589 --> 00:13:10,383
[Melon] Trouble sleeping?
Been eating all right?

267
00:13:10,884 --> 00:13:11,927
Uh...

268
00:13:12,010 --> 00:13:13,803
[Melon] It must have been quite a shock.

269
00:13:13,887 --> 00:13:16,139
A young one like you
witnessing something like that.

270
00:13:16,848 --> 00:13:17,974
Oh...

271
00:13:18,058 --> 00:13:19,684
Yeah, but I'm fine.

272
00:13:20,602 --> 00:13:23,730
It's just that I don't know
what I should do.

273
00:13:24,773 --> 00:13:26,983
[Melon] You mentioned
you saw someone, right?

274
00:13:27,067 --> 00:13:28,235
Yeah.

275
00:13:28,944 --> 00:13:31,821
It could be my imagination,
it was so fast.

276
00:13:31,905 --> 00:13:34,241
- [Melon] Did you tell the police?
- No, I didn't.

277
00:13:36,284 --> 00:13:37,285
Still though...

278
00:13:40,205 --> 00:13:42,165
I do wonder, if...

279
00:13:42,707 --> 00:13:44,209
[Melon] Huh.

280
00:13:44,292 --> 00:13:45,544
So if I'm not mistaken,

281
00:13:45,627 --> 00:13:48,672
you have a theory that someone
might have pushed the professor?

282
00:13:48,755 --> 00:13:49,881
Maybe.

283
00:13:49,965 --> 00:13:52,676
[Melon] What about suicide? An accident?

284
00:13:52,759 --> 00:13:55,887
Well, I found this feather, by the body.

285
00:13:55,971 --> 00:13:59,516
- [Melon] Hmm. A pigeon, perhaps?
- [mysterious music playing]

286
00:13:59,599 --> 00:14:00,850
Someone was there.

287
00:14:01,393 --> 00:14:03,645
[Melon] So this pigeon was involved?

288
00:14:04,271 --> 00:14:07,232
[sighs] I know it's not concrete evidence.

289
00:14:07,315 --> 00:14:08,149
[exhales]

290
00:14:08,233 --> 00:14:10,944
[Melon] So if we assume this was a crime...

291
00:14:11,486 --> 00:14:12,404
Um...

292
00:14:12,487 --> 00:14:17,367
[Melon] ...then that means whoever did this
is still out there on the loose.

293
00:14:18,535 --> 00:14:20,871
They might be out there plotting
and scheming

294
00:14:20,954 --> 00:14:22,789
to take down the next target.

295
00:14:23,456 --> 00:14:25,959
If they think you saw what they did,

296
00:14:26,042 --> 00:14:28,295
their sights could be set on you.

297
00:14:28,378 --> 00:14:30,547
Oh... Hmm...

298
00:14:30,630 --> 00:14:32,632
[mysterious music continues]

299
00:14:32,716 --> 00:14:36,219
{\an8}Oh, I get it now. I'm just being dramatic.

300
00:14:36,303 --> 00:14:37,220
[Melon] Huh?

301
00:14:37,846 --> 00:14:39,723
T-Thank you, I get what you're saying.

302
00:14:39,806 --> 00:14:43,476
My imagination is getting the better of me
and I'm overthinking it.

303
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:45,145
- [Melon] Uh...
- I've almost been killed

304
00:14:45,228 --> 00:14:46,313
a few times before, so...

305
00:14:46,396 --> 00:14:49,858
[chuckling] ...of course my brain
is jumping straight to murder.

306
00:14:49,941 --> 00:14:52,110
It must be a dwarf rabbit thing.
Know what I mean?

307
00:14:52,193 --> 00:14:54,237
- [Melon] Uh, yeah. [laughs]
- [laughs]

308
00:14:54,321 --> 00:14:56,489
If the police are saying
it was an accident,

309
00:14:56,573 --> 00:14:57,908
who am I to question them?

310
00:14:57,991 --> 00:15:01,161
[Melon] Hmm.
Do you think it could have been suicide?

311
00:15:01,244 --> 00:15:02,996
I guess I wouldn't know.

312
00:15:03,079 --> 00:15:06,666
However, if it was suicide,
she must have known she had other options.

313
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:10,420
[Melon] Huh, don't people commit suicide
when they think they're out of options?

314
00:15:11,087 --> 00:15:15,050
If you commit suicide, it must mean
you know you'll be alive tomorrow.

315
00:15:15,133 --> 00:15:17,761
- [Melon] Hmm.
- That's why I don't understand it.

316
00:15:17,844 --> 00:15:21,681
I've lived every day thinking
it might be the last day that I'm alive.

317
00:15:21,765 --> 00:15:25,894
[Melon] If that's true,
why bother with trying to get a degree?

318
00:15:25,977 --> 00:15:28,021
If you think you're going to die anyway.

319
00:15:28,104 --> 00:15:31,608
[chuckling] Come on. It's not as bleak
as you are making it sound.

320
00:15:31,691 --> 00:15:33,693
It's like, even if I think I might die,

321
00:15:33,777 --> 00:15:35,946
there are still some things
I hope I might achieve.

322
00:15:36,029 --> 00:15:37,656
I still have goals and dreams.

323
00:15:37,739 --> 00:15:40,492
[Melon] <i>This little one intrigues me.</i>

324
00:15:41,326 --> 00:15:45,497
<i>Even through her foreboding
and her mortal dread,</i>

325
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:49,459
<i>she's not willing throw away her chance
at a good life.</i>

326
00:15:49,542 --> 00:15:52,712
I guess I should talk to the police
just in case.

327
00:15:53,380 --> 00:15:55,048
I'm so glad you invited me here.

328
00:15:55,674 --> 00:15:56,841
Thank you very much.

329
00:15:57,384 --> 00:15:59,928
[Melon] Yeah, very well then.
[chuckles softly].

330
00:16:00,011 --> 00:16:01,638
Oh? [sniffs]

331
00:16:02,806 --> 00:16:04,140
It smells like rain.

332
00:16:05,308 --> 00:16:07,018
Looks like rain will be here soon.

333
00:16:08,144 --> 00:16:12,065
[Melon]
<i>Haru, the Botany Department freshman.</i>

334
00:16:14,275 --> 00:16:17,028
If you're going to the police,
I should take you.

335
00:16:17,112 --> 00:16:18,279
[Haru] What?

336
00:16:18,363 --> 00:16:20,699
[Melon] You shouldn't do
something like this by yourself.

337
00:16:20,782 --> 00:16:23,034
Don't worry, I can drive us.

338
00:16:23,618 --> 00:16:26,121
And like you said, the rain's on its way.

339
00:16:26,204 --> 00:16:28,623
[ominous music playing]

340
00:16:28,707 --> 00:16:30,083
[thunderclap]

341
00:16:30,166 --> 00:16:33,503
[Boss panting]

342
00:16:34,754 --> 00:16:36,548
[Kolo] Come on, Boss, hop on.

343
00:16:37,048 --> 00:16:39,759
[Boss grunting in exertion] Thanks!

344
00:16:39,843 --> 00:16:41,469
Wonder if he's already here.

345
00:16:41,553 --> 00:16:43,054
Just keep your cool.

346
00:16:43,138 --> 00:16:46,808
I'm excited to see our friend too,
but let's not make fools of ourselves.

347
00:16:46,891 --> 00:16:48,476
Yeah, you are right.

348
00:16:49,227 --> 00:16:53,690
But being so mature all day long
is not the easiest thing in the world.

349
00:16:53,773 --> 00:16:55,400
It's getting kind of exhausting.

350
00:16:55,483 --> 00:16:57,027
I hear ya on that one.

351
00:16:57,110 --> 00:17:00,238
Still, let's try to keep it cool today.
We are not freshmen.

352
00:17:00,321 --> 00:17:01,406
Yeah, that's true.

353
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:05,702
[Jack excitedly] Oh, there he is!

354
00:17:07,162 --> 00:17:09,581
Hey! Look who's here!

355
00:17:11,416 --> 00:17:13,334
[softly] Stay cool, guys.

356
00:17:13,418 --> 00:17:14,961
- [Kolo and Durham] Cool.
- [Boss] Yeah, got it.

357
00:17:16,129 --> 00:17:17,213
All right.

358
00:17:18,089 --> 00:17:20,508
[gentle music playing]

359
00:17:25,388 --> 00:17:27,265
[all panting]

360
00:17:27,348 --> 00:17:30,060
[panting, laughs]

361
00:17:30,143 --> 00:17:36,900
- [Legoshi laughing]
- [all speaking excitedly]

362
00:17:36,983 --> 00:17:40,653
{\an8}I tried to keep my cool,
but come on, can you guys blame me?

363
00:17:40,737 --> 00:17:43,990
{\an8}- What's it like living by yourself?
- [chuckles] Well, there's ups and downs.

364
00:17:44,074 --> 00:17:45,742
I've been sleeping in your bed, Legoshi!

365
00:17:46,367 --> 00:17:50,080
{\an8}So, what do you say?
Time to get wild, right?

366
00:17:50,163 --> 00:17:50,997
{\an8}[all howling]

367
00:17:51,081 --> 00:17:52,582
{\an8}- [Miguno] That's it!
- [Durham] Yeah!

368
00:17:52,665 --> 00:17:54,375
{\an8}Time to let loose!

369
00:17:54,459 --> 00:17:56,461
{\an8}- Off the hizzy!
- Let's go wild!

370
00:17:56,544 --> 00:17:58,254
{\an8}All the wild, none of the shame.

371
00:17:58,338 --> 00:17:59,881
{\an8}[Kolo] You are talking my language.

372
00:17:59,964 --> 00:18:02,383
{\an8}I don't know
about giving in to my instincts, though...

373
00:18:02,467 --> 00:18:05,345
{\an8}- [Jack] Don't worry, it's a safe space.
- Right...

374
00:18:07,013 --> 00:18:10,600
[Leisure facility announcer] <i>I want
to welcome our B-Strike visitors today.</i>

375
00:18:10,683 --> 00:18:12,435
<i>Go have some fun!</i>

376
00:18:12,519 --> 00:18:13,353
{\an8}[kangaroos snoring]

377
00:18:13,436 --> 00:18:14,270
{\an8}KANGAROO CORNER

378
00:18:14,354 --> 00:18:18,441
{\an8}[Legoshi] <i>Letting your wild instincts
creep into your daily life is pretty...</i>

379
00:18:18,525 --> 00:18:19,484
{\an8}<i>taboo.</i>

380
00:18:19,567 --> 00:18:20,568
{\an8}[all yelling]

381
00:18:20,652 --> 00:18:21,569
{\an8}FELINE CORNER

382
00:18:21,653 --> 00:18:23,613
{\an8}[Legoshi] <i>That's why it's important
that every species</i>

383
00:18:23,696 --> 00:18:26,324
{\an8}<i>has a place to let all their urges out.</i>

384
00:18:27,617 --> 00:18:28,451
{\an8}SQUIRREL CORNER

385
00:18:28,535 --> 00:18:31,371
{\an8}[Legoshi]
<i>Which is why B-Strike is so popular.</i>

386
00:18:31,454 --> 00:18:33,456
{\an8}[all panting]

387
00:18:34,290 --> 00:18:36,042
{\an8}CANINE CORNER

388
00:18:36,126 --> 00:18:37,168
{\an8}[Jack] This is it.

389
00:18:39,045 --> 00:18:40,880
[lights chime]

390
00:18:40,964 --> 00:18:41,798
[light countdown pinging]

391
00:18:42,423 --> 00:18:44,384
Oh, the anticipation is real.

392
00:18:44,467 --> 00:18:47,345
- My tail's going to wag right off.
- I will not lose!

393
00:18:47,428 --> 00:18:48,805
Me neither!

394
00:18:48,888 --> 00:18:51,224
[Miguno]
Hey, Legoshi, tired of living alone yet?

395
00:18:51,307 --> 00:18:53,518
[Legoshi]
Sometimes it gets a bit too quiet.

396
00:18:53,601 --> 00:18:55,478
But it makes times like this fun!

397
00:18:55,562 --> 00:18:58,815
Yeah, pretty soon we're gonna be too busy
with all our exams.

398
00:18:58,898 --> 00:19:00,984
Oh, I forgot, entrance exams.

399
00:19:01,734 --> 00:19:03,444
- [Legoshi] Oh!
- [Boss whoops]

400
00:19:03,528 --> 00:19:04,404
[male canine laughs]

401
00:19:04,487 --> 00:19:08,658
- [all panting and shouting excitedly]
- [upbeat music playing]

402
00:19:08,741 --> 00:19:09,909
- [indistinct shouting]
- [Kolo] Woah!

403
00:19:09,993 --> 00:19:11,035
[both grunt]

404
00:19:11,119 --> 00:19:12,453
[grunts in pain]

405
00:19:13,246 --> 00:19:14,455
Oh, that's mine!

406
00:19:15,081 --> 00:19:17,167
[straining] I got it!

407
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:19,794
- Come on, toss it back!
- Is it okay if I do it?

408
00:19:19,878 --> 00:19:20,920
- Do it!
- Let's go!

409
00:19:21,004 --> 00:19:22,797
- Yeah, it's your ball!
- Let loose!

410
00:19:22,881 --> 00:19:24,299
[panting]

411
00:19:24,382 --> 00:19:27,177
[Legoshi] <i>Bringing a ball
back to where it came from...</i>

412
00:19:27,802 --> 00:19:30,513
<i>Only canines understand. What a rush!</i>

413
00:19:31,598 --> 00:19:32,515
CONGRATULATIONS

414
00:19:32,599 --> 00:19:36,436
[female voice on machine] <i>Amazing!
Your return is today's fastest record!</i>

415
00:19:36,519 --> 00:19:40,440
<i>Congratulations on being number one!
You are so special!</i>

416
00:19:40,523 --> 00:19:41,357
[all cheering]

417
00:19:41,441 --> 00:19:44,485
I'm a good boy!

418
00:19:44,569 --> 00:19:45,695
Yes! Yeah!

419
00:19:45,778 --> 00:19:49,282
[Legoshi]
<i>Now, this is the life of a canine!</i>

420
00:19:49,365 --> 00:19:50,700
[upbeat music fades out]

421
00:19:50,783 --> 00:19:51,951
[Boss] Ah...

422
00:19:52,535 --> 00:19:54,913
[Jack] We're definitely gonna be
sore tomorrow. [chuckles]

423
00:19:54,996 --> 00:19:57,081
[Miguno] Is it weird that I don't care?

424
00:19:58,958 --> 00:20:00,043
So, guys...

425
00:20:01,461 --> 00:20:03,004
have you all picked a career?

426
00:20:03,087 --> 00:20:05,506
Seems like
we have to make our minds up soon.

427
00:20:05,590 --> 00:20:07,550
We can't all be outlaws like you.

428
00:20:07,634 --> 00:20:10,053
[chuckling]
You know, I'm thinking about it too.

429
00:20:10,637 --> 00:20:12,055
Durham, you sticking with swimming?

430
00:20:12,138 --> 00:20:15,058
Mmm, guess so. I got recommended.

431
00:20:15,141 --> 00:20:17,101
Boss is taking over the family business.

432
00:20:17,185 --> 00:20:18,561
[Boss] Yeah, that's right.

433
00:20:19,395 --> 00:20:23,399
[Legoshi] <i>Eventually, I guess,
we all have to find our own paths.</i>

434
00:20:24,359 --> 00:20:26,361
<i>It's not like we didn't know
it would happen.</i>

435
00:20:27,779 --> 00:20:30,782
<i>I just thought that, somehow,</i>

436
00:20:31,658 --> 00:20:33,451
<i>we'd always be together</i>

437
00:20:34,410 --> 00:20:36,579
<i>back in room 701.</i>

438
00:20:39,249 --> 00:20:41,000
[grunting with effort]

439
00:20:42,001 --> 00:20:45,255
Hey, guys,
do you think after we're all adults,

440
00:20:46,214 --> 00:20:48,299
we'll still hang out like this sometimes?

441
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:49,634
Uh...

442
00:20:50,176 --> 00:20:52,053
What are you talking about?

443
00:20:52,136 --> 00:20:53,554
- Of course we will.
- [male canine chuckling] Yeah.

444
00:20:53,638 --> 00:20:55,890
- All of us are canines for life, right?
- [all chuckling]

445
00:20:55,974 --> 00:20:58,184
All you need to do is howl
and we'll all be there!

446
00:20:58,268 --> 00:21:00,979
- [Miguno] That goes without saying!
- [indistinct]

447
00:21:01,062 --> 00:21:01,896
[all laughing]

448
00:21:06,442 --> 00:21:08,653
Looking forward
to seeing your place, Lego-face.

449
00:21:09,279 --> 00:21:10,822
You do keep it clean, don't you?

450
00:21:11,406 --> 00:21:14,200
[Legoshi] Hmm?
There's not much there to tidy up.

451
00:21:14,284 --> 00:21:17,078
I'd invite everyone,
but the walls are so thin.

452
00:21:17,161 --> 00:21:20,540
[inhales] We'd make too much noise
for the neighbors.

453
00:21:20,623 --> 00:21:21,791
Yeah, we are loud.

454
00:21:22,333 --> 00:21:23,876
Well, I mean, I know how to behave myself.

455
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:26,087
Y'know, I got those good boy manners.
[chuckles]

456
00:21:26,170 --> 00:21:29,841
Eh... You had my grandpa yelling at you
last time you were over.

457
00:21:29,924 --> 00:21:32,635
[laughing] Come on,
I was only nine years old!

458
00:21:32,719 --> 00:21:34,095
All right, meet you there.

459
00:21:37,056 --> 00:21:37,890
[Legoshi] Hmm?

460
00:21:38,474 --> 00:21:41,019
Oh... Hmm...

461
00:21:43,855 --> 00:21:44,939
Hmm.

462
00:21:45,732 --> 00:21:48,609
HAZARDOUS MATERIALS LIST
CANINES: ONIONS

463
00:21:48,693 --> 00:21:49,861
[Legoshi] <i>It's strange.</i>

464
00:21:50,403 --> 00:21:51,904
<i>We've always been together.</i>

465
00:21:52,655 --> 00:21:55,366
<i>And I never thought
there'd be an end in sight.</i>

466
00:21:56,242 --> 00:21:59,829
<i>Who would have guessed
that Jack had a secret?</i>

467
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,707
[closing theme song playing]
